<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0">
  <head><title>Hex-crawl travel log (Pointliner demo)</title></head>
  <body>
    <outline text="# Hex-crawl travel log" _id="hex00001">
      <outline text="A solo explorer mapping unknown territory, hex by hex. The map is the outline itself: regions hold hexes, hexes hold what you found there. Terrain is drawn from a deck (each type comes up once, then the deck reshuffles), encounters are dice, and your supplies tick down as a running total. Every {…} pill is live, click one to run it. See hex-crawl.md for the walkthrough." _id="hex00002"/>
      <outline text="## Generators (the tools you carry)" _id="hex00010">
        <outline text="Terrain deck (click to draw the next hex's terrain): {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}" _id="hex00011"/>
        <outline text="Weather for the day (a light cycle, click to advance): {cycle: clear | overcast | rain | fog}" _id="hex00012"/>
        <outline text="Wandering encounter check (2d6, 9 or less is quiet): {2d6}" _id="hex00013"/>
        <outline text="If something stirs, what is it? {a lone traveler | tracks, fresh | a wary beast | a hidden cache | distant smoke | signs of a camp}" _id="hex00014"/>
        <outline text="Distance you can push before dusk, in hexes: {1d6}" _id="hex00015"/>
        <outline text="Rations in your pack at the start (a variable the days draw down): {rations := 14}" _id="hex00016"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## The map: the Greytine Vale, {= sum(supplies, subtree)} of {rations} rations spent" _id="hex00020">
        <outline text="This is the nesting the demo is really about. The Vale is a point. Each region under it is a point. Each hex under a region is a point, and each hex carries what you discovered plus a supplies-used property. Fold a region closed (the chevron left of its bullet) to see the map shrink to its edges, and open it again to bring the hexes back. Clicking the bullet is a different move: it zooms the document into that region alone." _id="hex00021"/>
        <outline text="Region: The Fenlands (west of the ford), {= sum(supplies)} rations spent" _id="hex00030">
          <outline text="Hex 0101 (entered): terrain {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}. A shallow crossing, reeds to the horizon. {prop supplies: 1}" _id="hex00031"/>
          <outline text="Hex 0102: terrain {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}. Encounter check {2d6}, you spot {a lone traveler | tracks, fresh | a wary beast | a hidden cache | distant smoke | signs of a camp}. {prop supplies: 2}" _id="hex00032"/>
          <outline text="Hex 0103: terrain {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}. Slow, sucking ground costs an extra ration. {prop supplies: 3}" _id="hex00033"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Region: The Ashen Ridge (climbing east), {= sum(supplies)} rations spent" _id="hex00040">
          <outline text="Hex 0201: terrain {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}. Thin air, a long view back over the fens. {prop supplies: 2}" _id="hex00041"/>
          <outline text="Hex 0202: terrain {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}. Encounter check {2d6}. A cairn marks the pass. {prop supplies: 2}" _id="hex00042"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Two scopes, one keyword. A region totals the hexes directly under it with `{= sum(supplies)}`. The Vale heading above reaches every hex at any depth with `{= sum(supplies, subtree)}`. Both live on the point whose children they count, which is the whole trick: a rollup beside the list reads nothing." _id="hex00050"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## The daily loop (one day, played through)" _id="hex00060">
        <outline text="Day 3. Weather: {cycle: clear | overcast | rain | fog}. You break camp at the edge of Hex 0103." _id="hex00061"/>
        <outline text="&gt; I strike east toward the ridge line, aiming to make the pass by dusk." _id="hex00062"/>
        <outline text="Push distance today: {1d6} hexes." _id="hex00063"/>
        <outline text="New hex terrain: {shuffle: forest | hills | marsh | ruins | river | open plain}." _id="hex00064"/>
        <outline text="Encounter check: {2d6}. On 10 or more, something crosses your path: {a lone traveler | tracks, fresh | a wary beast | a hidden cache | distant smoke | signs of a camp}." _id="hex00065"/>
        <outline text="=&gt; I reach the cairn at Hex 0202 as the light fails, and make camp cold. #thread/the-pass" _id="hex00066"/>
        <outline text="Supplies burned today (the day's own tally over its noted legs): {= sum(supplies)}." _id="hex00067">
          <outline text="Morning march (fenland edge). {prop supplies: 1}" _id="hex00068"/>
          <outline text="Afternoon climb (loose scree, slow going). {prop supplies: 2}" _id="hex00069"/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="## How to run it" _id="hex00070">
        <outline text="Draw terrain: click a terrain pill and it pulls the next card from its deck. Click the SAME pill repeatedly and it gives each terrain once before any repeats, then reshuffles and tells you it did. Each pill keeps its own bag, so two hexes can both open on marsh; the no-repeat promise is per pill, not across the map." _id="hex00071"/>
        <outline text="Roll an encounter: click a {2d6} pill to roll, click again to re-roll. It freezes its result so the log stays an honest record of what you got. Read it against the threshold on the same line (quiet on a low number, something stirs on a high one)." _id="hex00072"/>
        <outline text="Watch supplies add up: each hex carries a supplies property (the `{prop supplies: N}` pill). The `{= sum(supplies)}` pill sits ON the region point and totals the hexes directly under it, live, so editing a hex's number re-totals the region without any math on your part." _id="hex00073"/>
        <outline text="Grow the map: add a hex as a child point under a region (Tab to indent), give it a terrain draw, an encounter check, and a {prop supplies: N}. Add a whole new region as a sibling. The outline is the map, so the map grows by outlining." _id="hex00074"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
</opml>
